00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:26.640
mentioned daily goals. We're going to

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.720
pick three goals. And the way we choose

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:30.640
our three goals is important. Most

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.880
people set goals in one category. Maybe

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:33.320
they're all about fitness, or they're

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.200
all about productivity, or they're all

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:38.040
about their mindset. And then they will

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:40.080
wonder why they feel imbalanced in their

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.400
life. For example, why your body looks

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.760
great but your mental health is tanking,

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:45.520
why your business is growing but your

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:47.080
relationships are dying, or why your

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:49.680
meditation practice is deep but your

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:51.880
bank account is not. You are not a

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:54.120
single dimension being. You are a whole

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:55.840
complete ecosystem of your mind, and

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:58.280
your body, and your spirit. So, every

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:01.040
day you should feed all three in these

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:02.920
small, specific, and completable ways.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:05.080
Each day you choose one goal for your

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.640
mind, one goal for your body, and one

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.120
for your spirit. And each goal must be

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:10.800
small enough that you can complete it no

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:12.800
matter what your day looks like. What

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:14.400
does this look like in practice? Mind

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:16.040
goals are anything that sharpens your

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.000
thinking, grows your knowledge, or

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:20.160
strengthens your mental resilience. For

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:21.960
example, read 10 pages, listen to half a

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:23.920
podcast, learn three new words in

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:26.200
another language, write for 10 minutes,

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:28.160
practice a skill for 15 minutes, apply

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:30.360
to one new opportunity. Body goals are

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.160
anything that honors your physical

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:33.280
vessel. Our body is a temple, you guys.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.000
We have to take care of it. So, for

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.960
example, walk 7,000 steps, drink eight

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.880
glasses of water, do one 10-minute

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:41.920
YouTube workout video, or try a new

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:43.600
healthy recipe, dance to your playlist

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:45.760
while you do makeup, and get to bed at a

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:47.520
specific time. Spirit goals are anything

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:49.640
that connects you to something deeper

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:52.080
than just your simple to-do list. For

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.720
example, 5 minutes of meditation,

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:55.240
calling someone that you love today, ask

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:56.920
them how they're doing, write a

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:58.600
gratitude letter to yourself or to

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:00.160
someone that you're grateful for. Maybe

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:01.600
that's a journal entry that you won't

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.400
send. It doesn't matter. It's all for

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.080
you. Or you can even sit in silence for

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.720
a little bit and spend time in nature

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:08.640
with no phone, practice surrender and

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.520
forgiveness towards yourself or towards

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.000
somebody else. And again, you're doing

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:14.120
this for you because the other person

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:16.839
may never deserve your kindness, but you

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:19.720
do. And create something with no goal

00:11:16.839 --> 00:11:22.040
other than just simply self-expression.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:23.440
Now, here's the key. On your best days,

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:25.800
your three goals might be ambitious,

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:27.440
like read 30 pages or do a 45-minute

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:29.720
workout or journal for 20 minutes, which

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:31.480
is very beautiful. Go for it. Some

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:33.200
people do 75 hard to challenge

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:34.480
themselves, and that's really great. It

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:36.320
really helps us build our mental

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:38.200
capacity and when we complete it, it

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.880
builds our confidence. On your worst

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.880
days though, your three goals still need

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:43.960
to be completable. Like read one

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:45.920
paragraph, stretch for two minutes, take

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:48.520
three deep breaths this morning. This is

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:50.640
literally the bare minimum. The goal is

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:53.280
not to be perfect of course, but no

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:54.400
matter what, we never break this chain.

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:56.080
Because the moment you skip a day

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.840
completely, which by the way is fine,

00:11:56.080 --> 00:12:00.320
but your brain may register this as

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:02.040
permission to skip the next day. And

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:03.760
then the next one and suddenly your

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:06.000
30-day transformation becomes like a

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.200
four-day experiment that you abandon and

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.880
we're not going to do that. So, on the

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:11.320
days where everything is falling apart

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:13.880
and you're exhausted and life is

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:15.600
life-ing, you still do your three things

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:18.600
because doing the bare minimum on a bad

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:20.280
day literally builds even more identity

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:22.880
level change than simply doing the

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:25.880
maximum on a good day. The tough days

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.520
are really a test to see if we can stick

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:28.760
with our ourselves. Now, you're doing

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:30.360
your routine, you're completing your

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.840
three goals across your mind, body and

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:33.200
spirit to build some momentum, but

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:36.360
here's where most people might start to

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:38.960
coast and unfortunately, coasting is

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:41.600
where radical change goes to die. Every

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:43.680
seven days or so, you can stop and reset

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:46.160
whatever works for your schedule. I do

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:48.360
it as I need to. Now, all you're doing

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.880
is a check-in with yourself. So, here's

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:51.800
what it looks like. Number one, review

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:54.000
your week. Honestly, how many of your

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:55.520
daily goals did you actually complete?

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.160
Don't judge yourself, just look at

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:59.800
what's in front of you and if you

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:02.280
completed 18 out of 21 goals and that's

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:04.640
like three per day for seven days, that

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:07.280
is an 86% completion rate, which is

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:09.920
incredible. But, if you complete nine

00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:11.880
goals out of 21, that's a sign that your

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:14.240
goals may probably be too ambitious for

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:16.160
where you are right now. So, now we know

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:18.280
and then we can scale down. Number two,

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:19.720
notice your patterns. Which dimension

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:21.280
did you skip the most? If you're

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:22.640
consistently skipping your spiritual

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:24.080
goals, that tells you something about

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:26.080
what you're avoiding and if your

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:27.120
physical body goals keep falling off,

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.960
that tells you something about your

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:31.160
relationship with your physical body.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:33.320
We're not doing anything wrong by not

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:36.280
completing anything. The patterns are

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:38.200
all information for you to learn from,

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:39.800
and again, we're not judging ourselves.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:41.520
Number three, write one thing that

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:43.320
surprised you. Maybe you found out that

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.560
you actually love taking a short walk

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.960
around the block in the morning, or

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:47.440
maybe you realized that reading before

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:49.880
bedtime is actually one of the most

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:51.880
peaceful and calming times of your day.

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:53.680
Or maybe you noticed that calling or

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:55.800
texting a friend or family member to

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:58.480
check in on them really made you feel

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:59.920
good. So, note down these new surprises.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:01.080
They are really clues about the life

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:03.480
that we're actually meant to be

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:05.800
building. Number four, set your

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:08.160
intentions for the next seven days.

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:10.000
Based on everything you learned, adjust

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:11.880
with small refinements. So, a bit more

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:14.280
of what worked and a lot less of what

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:16.000
felt like a chore to you. Now, I have to

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:17.880
address this because it's the reason

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:19.360
most people quit before day 30. You're

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:21.200
going to fall off. I'm not saying that

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:23.440
you might, I'm saying that you will,

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:25.080
literally. There will come a day where

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:26.720
you sleep through your alarm or your

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:28.360
anxiety is so loud you can't even sit

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.760
still, or life happens and you just

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:31.960
don't want to deal with anything. What

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:33.800
you do in that moment determines

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:35.320
everything that comes after that. Most

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:37.080
of these plans treat falling off like

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:38.880
you failed and you need to start over

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:40.280
again, and that one single belief has

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:42.480
destroyed more transformations than

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:44.520
laziness or feeling undisciplined ever

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:46.600
could. So, here's what I want you to do

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:49.200
instead. We can show ourselves more

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:51.080
compassion in these three ways. One,

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:53.120
acknowledge without dramatizing. For

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:55.360
example, you can say "I didn't do my

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:56.600
morning routine today." Period. Not,

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:58.440
"Oh, because I didn't do my morning

00:14:56.600 --> 00:15:00.280
routine I'm such a failure. I can't even

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:01.839
do 12 minutes. What's wrong with me? I'm

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:03.760
never going to change." We're not

00:15:01.839 --> 00:15:07.040
involving our emotions in this. We're

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:08.960
staying as neutral as possible. Two, ask

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:10.440
one question. "What did I need today

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:12.040
that I didn't give myself?" Maybe you

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:14.520
needed more sleep, maybe you needed to

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:17.520
cry out a bit, or to do absolutely

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:19.760
nothing. Those are your literal needs,

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:21.800
and it's also information for you to

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:23.680
know what to do next. I mean, sometimes

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:26.200
I don't get a bunch of sleep and my day

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:28.960
is thrown off. Fine, that's okay, not a

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:30.640
big deal. Three, return to the practice

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:32.280
literally the very next available

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:34.000
moment. If you miss your morning

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:35.440
routine, you can do a small routine

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:37.560
during your break, even if it's just one

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:39.600
thing. And if you missed all three

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:41.120
goals, do only one before bedtime. And

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:43.640
make it easy, you know, like instead of

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:45.280
reading 20 pages, read one line, and

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.720
read one sentence, read a paragraph. The

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:50.480
only rule is you don't let two days in a

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:52.880
row pass without returning to your plan.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:54.920
One day off is a rest day, but two days

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:57.040
off becomes a pattern. Now, I know what

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:59.200
some of you may be thinking, "May, I

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:01.240
need more tough love. I really need

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:03.040
someone to hold me accountable." And I

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:05.000
hear you, but here's what the research

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:07.440
actually shows. There are researchers at

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:09.200
UC Berkeley that ran four experiments on

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:12.000
this that had people reflect on personal

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:14.520
weaknesses, moral failures, and test

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:17.280
performance. The group that practiced

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:19.360
self-compassion actually became more

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:21.440
motivated to improve. They studied for

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:23.960
longer after failing a test. They

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:26.000
reported greater desire to make amends

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:28.480
after making a moral mistake. They were

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:30.640
also more likely to seek out other

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:32.240
people doing even better than them so

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:34.960
that they could learn from them.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:37.400
Self-criticism feels productive, and it

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:39.520
can even feel like accountability, but

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:41.960
what it actually does is activate your

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:44.080
threat response, floods your body with

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:46.720
stress cortisol, and make your brain

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:50.000
associate transformation with pain. And

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.920
our animal brain will always, always

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:54.880
move away from pain toward comfort. So,

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:57.360
the tougher you are on yourself, the

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:59.520
harder it becomes to bounce back. Just

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:00.600
because we're practicing compassion

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:02.600
doesn't mean that we're letting

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:05.560
ourselves off the hook. We're not doing

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:08.240
that. An actual self-compassion practice

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:10.240
is to take that hook out of your skin so

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:12.120
that you can actually move on. And if

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:14.199
you want to go deeper with your practice

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.600
and have me hold you accountable, I'm

00:17:14.199 --> 00:17:17.520
building something for you. So, Week

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:19.400
Angels 2.0 is a membership that I've

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:21.520
been developing over the last few months

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:23.240
that includes guided meditations,

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:25.400
nervous system regulation practices,

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:28.640
somatic techniques, and subliminals

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:30.840
designed to support exactly this kind of

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:32.840
transformation at the subconscious level

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:34.800
as well. So, not only will you have

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:36.840
access to all these great practices, you

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:39.000
will also have access to our community

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:40.760
where we can egg each other on, and I

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:42.680
will be in there as well egging you on.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:44.600
I'm launching the beta soon in a matter

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:46.600
of time. Well, when it's out, it's out.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:48.440
So, you know, if you want to be the

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:50.120
first person to get in, the waitlist

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:52.200
link is in the description. It's at

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:54.440
mayasuzuki.eo.page.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:55.920
When it drops, early supporters as well

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:58.000
as my current members, of course I

00:17:55.920 --> 00:18:00.160
appreciate my members endlessly, they

00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:01.720
will be the first to know. So, 30 days

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:03.800
from now, you can either be in the same

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:05.880
place as you are right now consuming

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:07.360
more content telling yourself that

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:09.640
you'll start when the timing is right,

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:11.640
or 30 days from now, you can be someone

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:13.280
who proved that they showed up for

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:15.760
themselves every single day

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:18.080
consistently, compassionately, and

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:19.280
completely. Our plan is simple. 12

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.800
minutes in the morning, three goals

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:23.080
across mind, body, and spirit, and every

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:24.600
7 days we check in on ourselves. We do

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.600
this for 30 days of you choosing

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:28.560
yourself, and that's it. Your rock

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:31.600
bottom is only the foundation that you

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:34.120
build everything else on, and this right

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:35.800
here can be how you start building. So,

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:37.320
drop a comment and tell me, what's your

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.920
day one going to look like? What are

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:40.600
your first three goals? And I want to

00:18:38.920 --> 00:18:42.040
hear them because this community, we

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:43.600
really hold each other through the

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:45.680
process, and we're really here to

